tions. A subscription that came from an offer keeps the pairs the offer had at signup. Prices of lines that ship are per delivery. Each option charges for all deliveries in its period. Changing the interval does not change the per-delivery price. maxItems: 12. uniqueItems: true. object.billing_interval_options[] (Value): {@see SubscriptionIntervalOptionInput}. A billing interval, such as every 2 months, that a plan, offer, or subscription lets buyers choose. Prices of lines that ship are per delivery, and each option charges for all deliveries in its period. Without a delivery cadence there is one delivery per period, so every option bills the same line prices once per period. With a delivery cadence, a longer period bills more deliveries of the lines that ship; other lines bill once per period. For a different price per interval with no delivery cadence, create separate plans. object.billing_schedule_owner (Required): string. Who supplies billing dates: flint advances the schedule after each paid renewal; external uses dates you supply. Change it with billing_schedule on PATCH /v1/subscriptions/{subscription_id}. Value enum: "flint", "external". object.billing_schedule_waiting_started_at (Optional): string. RFC3339 timestamp. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.cancel_at_period_end (Required): boolean. True when the subscription is scheduled to cancel at scheduled_cancel_at. Schedule with POST /v1/subscriptions/{subscription_id}/cancel; undo with PATCH and cancel_at_period_end false. object.canceled_at (Optional): string. RFC3339 timestamp. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.cancellation_details (Optional): {@see SubscriptionCancellationDetailsInput}. Who asked to cancel, when, and why. Present once a cancellation is requested, whether it takes effect at the end of the billing period or right away. Omitted when no one asked, and removed when a scheduled cancellation is undone. See cancellation_reason for voluntary and 