rned in place of a customer ID when the customer is expanded. object.customer.anyOf[2] (Value): null. object.customer_id (Required): string. The customer this subscription bills. Example: "cus_01KEZF7C006X9JK6NZNA2SM9XD". object.deliveries_per_period (Required): integer. Deliveries paid for by one billing period, from 1 to 24. One when no separate delivery cadence is set. Prices of lines that ship are per delivery. Format: int32. minimum: 1. maximum: 24. object.delivery (Optional): {@see SubscriptionDeliveryInput}. Saved delivery preference with the current delivery method display. Write responses use the same display as GET: fixed shipping reflects the current method configuration, and quoted shipping shows the last paid shipping amount when available. A subscription's saved delivery preference: method, destination, recipient, shipping cost, and who last changed it. object.delivery_hold (Optional): {@see SubscriptionDeliveryHoldInput}. Current delivery issue that blocks collection. Mutually exclusive with upcoming_delivery_hold. A hold on a subscription's deliveries because its delivery method or destination no longer works, and who can fix it. object.delivery_interval (Required): string or null. Delivery cadence frozen from the plan. Null when no separate delivery cadence is set; one delivery is made per billing period. Value enum: "daily", "weekly", "monthly", "yearly", null. object.delivery_interval_count (Required): integer or null. Number of delivery intervals between deliveries. Null when no separate delivery cadence is set. Format: int32. minimum: 1. object.early_termination_fee_money (Optional): {@see MoneyValueInput}. The fee in the recorded contract terms. Present whenever those terms include a fee. It applies only to a cancellation before contract_end_at. Flint never charges it. Later plan changes do not change this fee. Monetary amount represented as integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency code. object.end_after (Required): {@see SubscriptionEndAfterInput} or null. Recorded automatic end condition. Null when no automatic end is set. Cycles count charged billing periods, including imported completed_cycles. Pauses and skips do not use cycles. Already-paid prepaid deliveries continue on their shifted dates, even beyond the end date, and cancellation waits for the last remaining delivery. Skipping defers a delivery without consuming its entitlement. Ending never refunds. object.end_after.anyOf[1] (Value): {@see SubscriptionEndAfterInput}. The subscription's automatic end condition, measured by charged billing cycles or a saved local calendar date. object.end_after.anyOf[2] (Value): null. object.expires_at (Required): string or null. Projected end under the current schedule and committed plan changes, including an earlier scheduled cancellation. A date limit preserves already-paid entitlement without requiring a future charge schedule. A reached cycle limit uses the last paid period end, or current_period_end_at when no paid history exists; that fallback includes any skip or pause extension. A cycle limit with cycles left needs a future charge schedule unless a known scheduled cancellation determines the end. Paid deliveries extend the end to the last paid delivery when it is later. An indefinite pause with paid deliveries owed makes the end unknown. Null when the end cannot be determined or the subscription is canceled. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.external_reference_id (Optional): string. Caller-owned identifier for this resource in an external system. maxLength: 255. Example: "warehouse-1842". object.gift_recipient (Required): {@see SubscriptionGiftRecipientInput} or null. Who receives the gift, when this is a gift subscription. customer_id stays the purchaser. Flint clears it when the subscription ends and when the purchaser's data is erased. Null when the subscription isn't a gift. object.gift_recipient.anyOf[1] (Value): {@see SubscriptionGiftRecipientInput}. Who receives a gift subscription. The customer stays the purchaser, who pays, gets receipts and reminders, and manages the subscription. delivery.recipient stays the ship-to address. object.gift_recipient.anyOf[2] (Value): null. object.idempotency_key (Optional): string or null. The Idempotency-Key of the request that created this resource. `null` when that request sent no key, Flint created the resource, the reader isn't the caller that created it (another app install, a buyer, or the merchant reading an app's or buyer's record), or the caller that created an older record is unknown. Filter its list with `idempotency_key` to find it. Recorded payloads, including replayed responses and webhook events, can return `null`. To find a key that a replay returns as `null`, read the resource. Buyer sessions on routes shared with merchants get `null`. `/v1/me` responses do not include this field. object.inventory_wait (Optional): {@see SubscriptionInventoryWaitInput}. Renewal or prepaid delivery waiting for stock. Buyers receive only started_at. A subscription renewal or prepaid delivery waiting for stock. object.is_awaiting_billing_schedule (Optional): boolean. True while an active or trialing subscription on an external billing schedule has no next billing date. object.last_payment_error (Optional): {@see PaymentErrorSummaryInput}. Latest renewal payment failure, present only while status is past_due and the latest payment failed. Buyer responses omit merchant remediation and sensitive decline signals. A summary of why a payment attempt failed, with a normalized error code, a message, the failure time, and remediation. object.line_items (Required): Array of {@see SubscriptionLineItemInput}. What each renewal bills. Plan edits do not change it. Adding, changing or swapping a line takes that variant's current catalog price, which then stays until the line changes again. object.line_items[] (Value): {@see SubscriptionLineItemInput}. An item included in a customer's recurring purchase. object.merchant_id (Required): string. ID of the merchant this resource belongs to. Example: "mer_01KEZF7C00KPYH1DDFPCCX3B6E". object.metadata (Optional): {@see MetadataMapInput}. Stored caller-owned key-value data. See `MetadataInput` for key, value, and size rules. Caller-owned key-value data stored on a resource. Keys starting with flint_ are reserved for Flint and are not returned. Writes follow the limits on MetadataInput and MetadataPatchInput; maps written before those limits may not satisfy them. object.missed_billing_at (Optional): string. The billing date whose payment failed, as an RFC3339 timestamp. Present only while status is past_due. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.next_billing_at (Optional): string. When Flint next starts a scheduled renewal charge, as an RFC3339 timestamp. Present only while a trialing or active subscription has a billing date and isn't set to cancel at the end of its period. Absent when no renewal is scheduled: a subscription in its final billing cycle ends at expires_at, a paused subscription resumes at scheduled_resume_at, a past_due one reports the failed billing date in missed_billing_at and retries at next_retry_at, an incomplete one retries at next_retry_at, a scheduled start begins at starts_at, one set to cancel ends at scheduled_cancel_at, and an external schedule awaiting a date reports is_awaiting_billing_schedule. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.next_delivery_at (Required): string or null. When the next prepaid delivery order is due, shifted by a timed pause. Null when the subscription has an indefinite pause, no delivery is scheduled, or the subscription is canceled. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.next_retry_at (Required): string or null. Recorded automatic payment retry time. Null when no retry time is available. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.open_renewal_order_id (Optional): string. ID of the paid renewal order whose shipment has not been dispatched. It keeps its committed delivery destination after preference changes and cancellation. Absent when no such renewal order exists. Only renewal orders count; the signup order is not included. Example: "ord_01KEZF7C0054GQKJ142A8X367A". object.outstanding_money (Optional): {@see MoneyValueInput}. Unpaid balance of the failed renewal order, including tax, shipping and discounts, after payments and credits. Present only while status is past_due and a positive balance remains. Monetary amount represented as integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency code. object.pause_reason (Optional): string. Why the subscription is paused: merchant for a pause made with your API key or dashboard, buyer for the buyer's own pause, delivery_action_required for a pause during or after a delivery hold, and payment_failed when renewal payment retries ran out and your dunning settings pause the subscription. Omitted when the subscription is not paused. Value enum: "buyer", "delivery_action_required", "merchant", "payment_failed". object.paused_at (Optional): string. RFC3339 timestamp. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.paused_delivery_hold (Required): {@see SubscriptionPausedDeliveryHoldInput} or null. The delivery hold that expired and paused the subscription. Null when no stored expiry reason exists, including a manual pause during an active hold, or the subscription is no longer paused for delivery action. object.paused_delivery_hold.anyOf[1] (Value): {@see SubscriptionPausedDeliveryHoldInput}. The delivery hold that expired and paused this subscription. A manual pause during an active hold is not an expiry. This field does not imply a refund. object.paused_delivery_hold.anyOf[2] (Value): null. object.payment_link_id (Optional): string. The payment link that started this subscription, when there was one. Example: "pl_01KEZF7C007WDMA5P9BPZ8J2AM". object.payment_method (Optional): {@see ExpandedPaymentMethodSummaryInput} or null. Present only when `expand` includes `payment_method`; `null` when expanded and there is no related payment method. object.payment_method.anyOf[1] (Value): {@see ExpandedPaymentMethodSummaryInput}. A payment method's summary fields, including type, status, and card details, returned when the payment method is expanded. object.payment_method.anyOf[2] (Value): null. object.payment_method_due_at (Required): string or null. First charge boundary while no card is bound: the later of trial_end_at and next_billing_at during a trial, or the next billing date for an imported period, even when that cycle's charge is zero. Recomputed when the schedule changes. A trial still without a card at its boundary cancels without an order or payment attempt. At that boundary, an imported subscription with a positive charge that still has no card enters its normal dunning schedule without a payment attempt. For an imported subscription, a zero charge completes the renewal without a card and the deadline advances to the following boundary. Null when a card is bound, collection is not scheduled (paused, canceled, or set to cancel at period end), an active or trialing subscription is in its final end_after cycle, or an external schedule has no known boundary. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.payment_method_id (Required): string or null. Saved payment method used for renewal charges. Null when no card is bound. Bind a card to this subscription with PATCH; changing the customer's default alone does not bind it. Example: "pm_01KEZF7C0034B248TXXE4NXYFZ". object.promotions (Required): Array of {@see SubscriptionPromotionInput}. Recurring promotions applying to the next charged cycle. Scheduled attachments are listed in scheduled_promotions. Empty when none apply; signup-only and exhausted promotions are excluded. object.promotions[] (Value): {@see SubscriptionPromotionInput}. A recurring promotion applied to a subscription, including its recurrence and remaining discounted cycles. object.prorate_first_period (Required): boolean. Whether this subscription was created to prorate its first anchored paid period. Set at creation and never changes; starting on the anchor day still bills a normal full period. object.recurring_subtotal_money (Required): {@see MoneyValueInput} or null. What one billing period's items cost before discounts, shipping, and tax: each line's price with modifiers, times quantity. It changes when items, quantity, or the plan change; editing the plan doesn't change it. For the next charge, use a subscription preview in next_renewal mode. `null` when a cancellation succeeds but Flint couldn't load the billing snapshot afterward, so the cancel response returns it as null. Retrieve the subscription again to get it. object.recurring_subtotal_money.anyOf[1] (Value): {@see MoneyValueInput}. Monetary amount represented as integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency code. object.recurring_subtotal_money.anyOf[2] (Value): null. object.remaining_cycles (Required): integer or null. Charges left for a cycle limit, bounded by an earlier scheduled cancellation. Null when there is no cycle limit or the subscription is canceled. Format: uint64. minimum: 0. object.remaining_prepaid_deliveries (Required): integer. Paid deliveries whose delivery order Flint hasn't created yet. A paid period starts with deliveries_per_period minus one. When delivery_hold is present and this count is positive, fixing delivery releases an already-paid delivery with shipping waived and no new charge. A next_renewal preview still estimates the next paid billing cycle. Skips, holds, and pauses consume none. Frozen on cancellation for manual refunds. Format: int32. minimum: 0. maximum: 23. object.resume_requested_at (Required): string or null. When Flint accepted a pending resume request. Set only while paused with a resume Flint has not applied yet. Clears when Flint resumes the subscription or refuses the request. `null` when the subscription isn't paused or no resume request is pending. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.scheduled_cancel_at (Required): string or null. When the scheduled cancellation takes effect: trial_end_at while trialing, current_period_end_at while active, or next_retry_at while past_due. Paid deliveries extend it to the last paid delivery when it is later. Null when cancel_at_period_end is false or no cancellation time is available. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.scheduled_plan_change (Required): {@see SubscriptionScheduledPlanChangeInput} or null. Frozen target terms for the next charged renewal. Null when no plan change is scheduled. Cancel with scheduled_plan_change: null on PATCH; replace through change-plan. object.scheduled_plan_change.anyOf[1] (Value): {@see SubscriptionScheduledPlanChangeInput}. Frozen target terms that apply at the next charged renewal. object.scheduled_plan_change.anyOf[2] (Value): null. object.scheduled_promotions (Required): Array of {@see SubscriptionPromotionInput}. Attached promotions whose first_cycle is after the next charged cycle, completed_cycles + 1. Always present; empty when no promotions are scheduled. object.scheduled_promotions[] (Value): {@see SubscriptionPromotionInput}. A recurring promotion applied to a subscription, including its recurrence and remaining discounted cycles. object.scheduled_resume_at (Required): string or null. When a pause with a length (pause_duration_cycles) resumes on its own: that many delivery intervals after paused_at on a prepaid subscription, or billing intervals otherwise. Null when the subscription is not paused or the pause has no length, such as a pause until you resume it or the pause Flint starts when a delivery hold runs out. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.service_location (Optional): {@see SubscriptionServiceLocationInput}. Omitted for a checkout session credential that doesn't act for the customer the buyer verified. The address wh